  "body": "Found by the work on #3567 (PR #3577, the ramp entry at a dead end).\n\n## What happens\nThe verifier `camcraft_sim::verify::verify_bodies` takes minutes for a 2D toolpath that goes down by ramps. Measured in debug on the test `pocket_pass_start::fig8_pocket_outside_starts_each_level_at_the_stock_edge`:\n\n| Tree | Time |\n|---|---|\n| `main` (4c0a157e1) | 89.6 s, pass |\n| PR #3577 at e7ae538a3 | more than 1500 s (stopped) |\n| the same with the ramp thinned to the arc-fit tolerance | more than 9 minutes (stopped) |\n\nThe planning and the emit of the path take 0.21 s (8850 moves, 33 passes). The time is in the verifier:\n- crossings: 0.0 s;\n- tangency: 34.7 s for 2232 moves that are not planar;\n- solid: 1 s;\n- `reach::band_reach` (`crates/sim/src/verify/reach.rs:72-80`): not complete after 3 minutes.\n\n## Cause\nEach ramp move ends at its own Z. `band_reach` slices the model at each different cut Z (`rest.islands_at`), adds the boundary samples of each slice to one sample set, and tests each move against the whole set. The cost is about moves x planes x samples. A path with helices, as on `main`, has few planes. The tangency check slices one time for each different Z also (about 15 ms each in debug).\n\nThe same cost can come from any path with many different Z values: a ramp entry that a user selects today, a helix with a small pitch, a 3D path. A user waits minutes with no progress and no message. The Prime Directive asks for a clean result, not a hang.\n\n## Wanted\n- `band_reach` keeps the island samples for each plane and tests a move only against the planes that it reaches (or an index by Z), so that the cost does not grow with moves x planes.\n- The cache key of `islands_at` and the tangency slices are checked for the same pattern.\n- A test with a ramp of many small moves pins a time or a count bound (a count of slice calls is better than wall time).\n- The findings of the verifier do not change: pin them on the existing cases (this is a collision and gouge check, under the safety floor).\n\n## Why P2\nPR #3577 (the fix of #3567) cannot merge before this: with it, a 2D Offset or 2D Pocket with Pass starts at Outside takes minutes to verify. Measure the release build also and correct the priority if it is seconds there.\n",
